WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.280
Bowen's series describes crystallization order as magma cools. In the discontinuous

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:12.210
branch, follow olivine, pyroxene, amphibole, then biotite. High-temperature minerals appear first.

00:00:13.017 --> 00:00:18.826
Plagioclase changes from calcium-rich toward sodium-rich. Potassium feldspar, muscovite, and quartz

00:00:18.826 --> 00:00:21.467
belong toward the low-temperature end.

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:26.805
Now reverse the reasoning. On heating, lower-melting components enter the liquid

00:00:26.805 --> 00:00:31.343
first. Partial melt is generally more silica-rich than its source, while

00:00:31.343 --> 00:00:32.581
solid minerals remain.
